NNAAMMEE
       demo - exercise every roffsub element

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ddeemmoo [--rr] [--kk _l_i_s_t] [_f_i_l_e ...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddeemmoo reads each _f_i_l_e in turn, or the standard input when none is named,
       and writes the records it finds in the order chosen by the options. A
       space written as a backslash space, as in a b c, never breaks. Fonts may
       change mid word, as in ssrrtt(1) and _f_i_l_e.txt.

       A second paragraph follows the first after one blank line, and it is long
       enough to wrap at every width the reference outputs use, which is the
       point of it.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --rr     reverse the emitted order.

       --kk _l_i_s_t
              sort by the columns in _l_i_s_t, then the remaining columns in order.

       ----rreessppeecctt--bbllaannkkss
              treat each indented block as a unit; the tag is longer than the
              indent, so the body starts on the next line.

       --xx  a width of four sets the prevailing indent, which the next item
           keeps.

       --oo _f_i_l_e
           write to _f_i_l_e instead of the standard output.

   LLiissttss
       o      bullets use the bullet character, shown as o on an ASCII terminal.

       o      a second bullet item.

       1.  a numbered item with its own width.

       2.  a second numbered item.

   NNeessttiinngg
       Text before a nested block.
              Nested text sits one prevailing indent further in.
                 A deeper block, moved in by three cells.
              Back at the first level.
       Back at the section margin.
       After a line break, still the same paragraph.


       After two blank lines.

TTAABBLLEE
        OOPPTTIIOONN   MMEEAANNIINNGG
       --------+-------------------
        --rr       reverse the order
        --kk _K_E_Y   sort on _K_E_Y

       A boxed table with a text block:
       -------+----------------------------------------------------------+------
        NNAAMMEE    DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN                                                SSIIZZEE
       -------+----------------------------------------------------------+------
        alpha   a long description that has to wrap when the terminal is     12
                narrow, kept inside its column
        beta    short                                                      3456
       -------+----------------------------------------------------------+------

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       demo -k5,3 file
       demo -r < input > output

